R.1  THE ASSERTION

     The act of distinction.  Representing the six contents forces
     the mediated composite S0 = X (x) !X, and !X stands without an
     act of its own (Axiom 2.2).  One mediation (Axiom 4.1).

       6 assertions, one for each content
       1 mediation
       6 structural opposites, forced, charged nothing
       ----
       7 acts, and all 2^6 = 64 addresses stand within the descent

     The boundaries.  Each clause is a bounded relation of capacity
     k = 3 (Theorem 7.2), and its excluded sector is its own three
     contents at the opposite orientation (Theorem 8.1), written in
     three symbols and forced rather than asserted.

         #  clause                 excluded sector            symbols
         0  !x1 v !x2 v x3         x1=T, x2=T, x3=F           3
         1  !x1 v x3 v !x6         x1=T, x3=F, x6=T           3
